      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. It's 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. Doses this high raise the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum)\n- **1700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg twice daily or 1000 mg twice daily\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me that and give me a short rationale for the order note. I'd still suggest confirming it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
